---
title: Switch & switcher
description: A switch turns one thing on or off. A switcher chooses one of a few, with a thumb that slides to the choice — the theme control, a style toggle, monthly or yearly. Both are real form inputs.
eyebrow: Component
source: src/components/feedback.css · switcher.css
---
<h2>Switcher</h2>
<p>Real radio buttons in a <code>&lt;fieldset&gt;</code>: a form can submit it, the arrow keys move it, a screen reader says "2 of 3". The thumb is positioned by CSS alone, from <em>which</em> radio is checked.</p>
{{#example center=true}}
<fieldset class="im-switcher" aria-label="Billing">
	<label><input type="radio" name="sw-bill" checked><span>Monthly</span></label>
	<label><input type="radio" name="sw-bill"><span>Yearly</span></label>
</fieldset>
<fieldset class="im-switcher" aria-label="View">
	<label><input type="radio" name="sw-view" checked>{{> "icons/layout-grid"}}<span>Grid</span></label>
	<label><input type="radio" name="sw-view">{{> "icons/rows-3"}}<span>List</span></label>
	<label><input type="radio" name="sw-view">{{> "icons/calendar"}}<span>Archive</span></label>
</fieldset>
{{/example}}

<h3>As the theme switcher</h3>
<p>Add <code>data-theme-set</code> to each radio and <code>im.js</code> wires it to the page's theme — and keeps it checked to match. Both of these are live.</p>
{{#example center=true}}
{{> "components/theme-switch"}}
{{> "components/theme-switch" icons=true}}
{{/example}}
{{{{code "hbs"}}}}
{{> "components/theme-switch"}}          {{!-- size="sm" | "lg" · icons=true --}}

{{!-- which is this, written out --}}
<fieldset class="im-switcher" aria-label="Theme">
	<label><input type="radio" name="im-theme" value="light" data-theme-set="light">{{> "icons/sun"}}<span>Light</span></label>
	<label><input type="radio" name="im-theme" value="dark" data-theme-set="dark">{{> "icons/moon"}}<span>Dark</span></label>
</fieldset>
{{{{/code}}}}
<p><strong>Two themes, not three.</strong> There is no "Auto" option to choose and no third state to store: a visitor who has never chosen is shown what their system asks for and goes on following it, and the first press settles it for good. A switch with three options makes the reader answer a question about their own operating system that the page can answer for them.</p>
<p>For a single button that flips between the two instead, there is <code>partials/components/theme-button.hbs</code> — the one in this site's top bar.</p>

<h3>Variants</h3>
{{#example}}
<div class="im-stack im-stack-sm" style="align-items: flex-start">
	<fieldset class="im-switcher im-switcher-sm" aria-label="Small"><label><input type="radio" name="sw-a" checked><span>Day</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="sw-a"><span>Week</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="sw-a"><span>Month</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="sw-a"><span>Year</span></label></fieldset>
	<fieldset class="im-switcher im-switcher-solid" aria-label="Solid"><label><input type="radio" name="sw-b" checked><span>Grid</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="sw-b"><span>List</span></label></fieldset>
	<fieldset class="im-switcher im-switcher-lg" aria-label="Large"><label><input type="radio" name="sw-c"><span>For readers</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="sw-c" checked><span>For writers</span></label></fieldset>
	<fieldset class="im-switcher im-switcher-block im-max-sm" aria-label="Full width"><label><input type="radio" name="sw-d" checked><span>Sign in</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="sw-d"><span>Create account</span></label></fieldset>
</div>
{{/example}}
<p><code>-sm</code> · <code>-lg</code> · <code>-solid</code> (the thumb takes the ink) · <code>-icons</code> (labels kept for screen readers) · <code>-block</code>. Two to five options; more than that is a <a href="/forms/controls/">select</a>.</p>

<h2>Switch</h2>
{{#example center=true}}
<label class="im-switch"><input type="checkbox" role="switch" checked><span>Email me new posts</span></label>
<label class="im-switch"><input type="checkbox" role="switch"><span>Weekly digest</span></label>
<label class="im-switch"><input type="checkbox" role="switch" disabled><span>Disabled</span></label>
{{/example}}
<p>A real checkbox with <code>role="switch"</code>. The thumb stretches while held, then springs across. In a settings list:</p>
{{#example style="max-width: 28rem"}}
<div class="im-stack" style="--im-stack-gap: 0">
	<label class="im-switch flex justify-between py-3"><span>Comments<small class="block text-xs text-muted">Let members reply under posts</small></span><input type="checkbox" role="switch" checked style="order: 2"></label>
	<hr class="im-divider">
	<label class="im-switch flex justify-between py-3"><span>Reading time<small class="block text-xs text-muted">Shown beside the date on every post</small></span><input type="checkbox" role="switch" style="order: 2"></label>
</div>
{{/example}}

<h2>Switch or switcher or checkbox?</h2>
<ul>
	<li><strong>Switch</strong> — one setting, on or off, that takes effect <em>at once</em>.</li>
	<li><strong>Switcher</strong> — one of a few mutually exclusive options, all visible.</li>
	<li><strong><a href="/forms/choices/">Checkbox</a></strong> — a choice that is submitted with a form, or several that can be on together.</li>
</ul>
